  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 247 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nThe upper low will lift northeast across the southern Rockies \nSunday night and into the northern Plains by Monday evening.\nSouthwest flow aloft will persist across the area behind the\ndeparting upper system, with the potential for several minor \ndisturbances moving through aloft. Scattered showers and a few\nstorms will be possible primarily across far western counties   \nMonday and Monday night, and across much of the area on Tuesday. \nHowever, not everyone will see rain, as showers and storms\nshould be widely scattered. Daytime high through Tuesday will\nbe near normal with highs in the upper 70s to near 80 degrees, \nwhile overnight lows will be above normal, with lows in the \nupper 50s and lower 60s. \n\nWednesday looks dry as upper level support will be lacking.\nShould see less cloud cover as well, which will allow temperatures\nto warm into the low to mid 80s by afternoon. Rain chances will \nreturn to the area by Thursday and linger into Saturday, as we \nremain in southwest flow aloft and additional disturbances move \nacross the area. Still some uncertainty this far out, so additional\nchanges to the forecast are likely in the coming days.",
